About the role

A Snapshot of Your Day!

The role is essential for maintaining and enhancing strategic assets of Sales and Service business functions which are central to the Transformation of Industry's digital services. To meet these objectives, the role will focus on two core areas: advanced AI application development and robust solution architecture. This involves hands-on development using Generative AI and RAG frameworks, as well as managing the full application lifecycle from design and deployment to maintenance and continuous improvement. Given the focus on cutting-edge AI and application stability, the ideal candidate will possess advanced expertise in .NET, python, cloud platforms, and GenAI technologies. As a senior professional, you will be expected to work independently on complex problems, manage development processes, and provide technical guidance to other team members.

How You’ll Make an Impact.

Design, develop, and deploy scalable AI applications utilizing Generative AI (GenAI) and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) frameworks.
Maintain, troubleshoot, and enhance existing AI solutions, to ensure high availability and performance.
Implement and manage CI/CD pipelines to automate the testing and deployment of AI models and associated application components.
Manage the end-to-end lifecycle of AI applications, from data preprocessing and model training to API integration and production monitoring.
Define and document the technical architecture for new and existing AI systems, ensuring alignment with business requirements and scalability.
Evaluate and select appropriate technologies, cloud services (AWS/Azure), and frameworks for AI projects to optimize performance and cost.
Collaborate with product managers and business stakeholders to translate functional requirements into robust technical specifications.
Coach and review the work of junior engineers, promoting best practices in software engineering, MLOps, and secure coding.
What You Bring

Bachelor's or master’s degree in computer science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, or a related technical field.
8+ years of professional experience in software development, with a significant focus on building and deploying production-level AI/ML solutions.
5+ years of experience in building well architected REST API solutions in .NET and or Python Fast API.
Hands-on experience with Azure Cloud Services with expertise in Managed AI services in Azure. Familiarity with AWS is a plus.
Demonstrable experience developing applications using Large Language Models (LLMs), Generative AI, and RAG architecture.
Experience working in an agile environment and managing projects/processes with limited supervision.
AI & Data Science - Python (Programming Language), Generative AI, RAG Frameworks, SQL (Programming Language), Analytical Skills
Software & Cloud Engineering- Cloud Services, DevOps, CI/CD, Application Programming Interface (API), Microservices. Knowing Terraform is a plus.
Professional Abilities- Troubleshooting (Problem Solving), Agile Methodology
About the Team

Our Transformation of Industry division is decarbonizing the industrial sector. Increasing electrification and efficiency are key and demand for green H2 and derivative fuels will rise. We enable decarbonization of the industrial sector and the transition to sustainable processes, building on a strong industrial customer base, a global network, diverse technologies, and integrated execution capabilities. Candidates want to learn about the divisions they will be joining–the structure, how it works together, and the role it plays in driving Siemens Energy’s mission forward.

Who is Siemens Energy?

At Siemens Energy, we are more than just an energy technology company. With ~100,000 dedicated employees in more than 90 countries, we develop the energy systems of the future, ensuring that the growing energy demand of the global community is met reliably and sustainably. The technologies crafted in our research departments and factories drive the energy transition and provide the base for one sixth of the world's electricity generation.

Our distributed team is committed to making balanced, reliable, and affordable energy a reality by pushing the boundaries of what is possible. We uphold a 150-year legacy of innovation that encourages our search for people who will support our focus on decarbonization, new technologies, and energy transformation.

